# Keep internal / non-webroot files out of the image. nginx.conf also
# denies these at request time for deployments that copy the folder
# straight to a webroot without going through this build.
#
# nginx.conf itself is deliberately NOT listed: .dockerignore drops a
# file from the whole build context, which would also break the earlier
# `COPY nginx.conf ...` in the Dockerfile. Its webroot exposure is
# already handled by nginx.conf's own deny rule.
.git
.gitignore
.dockerignore
Dockerfile
Jenkinsfile
web.config
README.md
scripts
